      "text": "A bot monitor should distinguish desired operation, observed liveness, and demonstrated work progress. This design inference adapts Kubernetes status conventions and the gray-failure observation gap. Evidence records can preserve event time, observation time, source identity, and correlation context using the OpenTelemetry vocabulary. Missing evidence must remain distinguishable from a confirmed failure. The Freqtrade heartbeat-only report is disputed, and the issue retains both the reporter\u2019s allegation and the maintainer\u2019s challenge instead of establishing a bot defect. These are reusable design patterns and historical reports, not a verified deployment specification.",
